<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16321" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Euclīdes</span></b> , is,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Εὐκλείδης</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Greek proper
			name</i>, <i>Euclid.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A philosopher of Megara</i>, <i>a
				disciple of Socrates and founder of the Megaric sect</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Cic. Ac. 2, 42, 129</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Gell. 6,
				10, 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sid. Carm. 2,
			176</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A mathematician in Alexandria under Ptolemy
				Philadelphus</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 3, 33, 132</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
